From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Walsh <contact.me@thejustinwalsh.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:07:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] llama: moe expert cache looks the ids of a multi-token
 batch up as one flat row

0004 extended the cache chain to every batch the CPU computes (2..31 tokens:
MTP verify windows, several slots decoding together) but kept 0003's one-token
lookup, ggml_get_rows(table [1, n_expert], ids [n_expert_used, n_tokens]).
get_rows needs a->ne[2] == b->ne[1], which holds only for one token, so
every multi-token graph -- the -np N reserve graph first -- aborted at load
with GGML_ASSERT(a->ne[2] == b->ne[1]) (ggml.c:3973; the Flash-Next gate's
cache-strata arm, 2026-09-28). The ids are made contiguous and looked up as
one row of n_expert_used * n_tokens, then viewed back as [n_expert_used,
n_tokens]. One token: the same graph as before plus a no-op view.
---
 src/llama-graph.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/llama-graph.cpp b/src/llama-graph.cpp
index bb8998000ba8c795296039b4d7b25078937ee6bd..106927d8d39b1f16490622dfd4ec9e36ba807a94 100644
--- a/src/llama-graph.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-graph.cpp
@@ -2181,7 +2181,14 @@ ggml_tensor * llm_graph_context::build_moe_ffn(
         mcache = llama_moe_cache_lookup(up_exps);
     }
     if (mcache) {
-        mc_slot_ids = ggml_get_rows(ctx0, mcache->dev_table, selected_experts); // [1, n_expert_used, 1]
+        // ggml_get_rows(a, b) needs a->ne[2] == b->ne[1]: with the table [1, n_expert] that holds for one token
+        // only, so the [n_expert_used, n_tokens] ids are looked up as one flat row. Before this, every batch of
+        // 2..31 tokens (0004's multi-token graphs; the -np N reserve builds one) hit
+        // GGML_ASSERT(a->ne[2] == b->ne[1]) in ggml_get_rows. selected_experts is a view of the top-k, so it is
+        // made contiguous first (n_expert_used x n_tokens ids).
+        ggml_tensor * mc_ids = ggml_is_contiguous(selected_experts) ? selected_experts : ggml_cont(ctx0, selected_experts);
+        mc_ids      = ggml_reshape_1d(ctx0, mc_ids, n_expert_used * n_tokens);
+        mc_slot_ids = ggml_get_rows(ctx0, mcache->dev_table, mc_ids); // [1, n_expert_used * n_tokens]
         mc_slot_ids = ggml_reshape_2d(ctx0, mc_slot_ids, n_expert_used, n_tokens);
         cb(mc_slot_ids, "ffn_moe_cache_slots", il);
     }
